  "worked_solution": "Our task is to find $A,$ $B$ and $C$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-2{x}^{2}+29x+1}{(4x-1)(x+3)(x+1)} & =\\frac{A}{(4x-1)}+\\frac{B}{(x+3)}+\\frac{C}{(x+1)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $(4x-1)(x+3)(x+1)$ gives\n\n$$\n-2{x}^{2}+29x+1=A(x+3)(x+1)+B(4x-1)(x+1)+C(4x-1)(x+3).\n$$\n\nFor $x=\\frac{1}{4}$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2{(\\frac{1}{4})}^{2}+29(\\frac{1}{4})+1 & =A(\\frac{1}{4}+3)(\\frac{1}{4}+1) \\\\  & \\,+B(4(\\frac{1}{4})-1)(\\frac{1}{4}+1) \\\\  & \\,+C(4(\\frac{1}{4})-1)(\\frac{1}{4}+3) \\\\ -\\frac{1}{8}+\\frac{29}{4}+1 & =A(\\frac{65}{16}) \\\\ \\frac{65}{8} & =A(\\frac{65}{16}) \\\\ A & =\\frac{16}{8} \\\\ A & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=-3$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2(-3)^{2}+29(-3)+1 & =A(-3+3)(-3+1) \\\\  & \\,+B(4(-3)-1)(-3+1) \\\\  & \\,+C(4(-3)-1)(-3+3) \\\\ -18-87+1 & =B(-13)(-2) \\\\ B & =\\frac{-104}{26} \\\\ B & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=-1$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2(-1)^{2}+29(-1)+1 & =A(-1+3)(-1+1) \\\\  & \\,+B(4(-1)-1)(-1+1) \\\\  & \\,+C(4(-1)-1)(-1+3) \\\\ -2-29+1 & =C(-5)(2) \\\\ C & =\\frac{-30}{-10} \\\\ C & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\frac{-2{x}^{2}+29x+1}{(4x-1)(x+3)(x+1)}=\\frac{2}{(4x-1)}-\\frac{4}{(x+3)}+\\frac{3}{(x+1)}.\n$$",
